From: Nicolas Villar <15879262+nvillar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:18:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Duo: recover a committed predictive Back whose closing
 transition never arrives

A committed predictive Back that prepared a transition (cross-task, cross-activity, back to home) asks the app to go
back and waits for the closing transition that results: BackTransitionHandler keeps the prepare transition and sets
mCloseTransitionRequested, and core keeps the back animation composed until the closing transition finishes
(BackNavigationController.onTransactionReady sets mPrepareCloseTransition; onTransitionFinish clears). If the app's Back
changes nothing, no closing transition comes: Task.canMoveTaskToBack can reject the move (an activity controller veto
of the task that would resume next, lock task), a moveTaskToBack can be a no-op, or the transition can be aborted or
have no targets. Shell's animation timeout then finishes the gesture, but onAnimationFinished does not finish the
prepare transition while mCloseTransitionRequested is set, and onBackNavigationDone does not clear the composition in
core: the closing task keeps its post-commit transform, the opening target stays paused for touch
(WindowState.canReceiveTouchInput -> shouldPauseTouch) and every later predictive Back returns "Previous animation
hasn't finish" (ledger F22, residual after fw 0021/0022).

When the post-commit animation has finished and the closing transition has not arrived (no close was merged or
handled), BackTransitionHandler waits a bounded 1 s for it and then takes the existing cancel path: it clears
mCloseTransitionRequested and starts the close prepare transition (WindowContainerTransaction.restoreBackNavi). Core
restores the launch-behind targets (BackNavigationController.restoreBackNavigation), Shell finishes the held prepare
transition (merge, startAnimation or onTransitionConsumed of the close prepare transition, as for a cancelled gesture),
and core's onTransitionFinish of the prepare transition clears the animation (no mPrepareCloseTransition), which
releases the leashes and the touch pause. A closing transition that arrives within the bound is handled as before; one
that arrives later is played by the default handlers.

Not built or run on a device yet. Verified by git am -3 after the series and a javac type check against the gate
build's framework and WM Shell jars. Device test: tools/duo-gate/backveto (activity controller veto).

Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../shell/back/BackAnimationController.java   | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/back/BackAnimationController.java b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/back/BackAnimationController.java
index 532bec2f8..3a7bc5c00 100644
--- a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/back/BackAnimationController.java
+++ b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/back/BackAnimationController.java
@@ -111,6 +111,8 @@ public class BackAnimationController implements RemoteCallable<BackAnimationCont
      * Max duration to wait for an animation to finish before triggering the real back.
      */
     private static final long MAX_ANIMATION_DURATION = 2000;
+    /** Duo: how long a committed Back waits for its closing transition after the post-commit animation. */
+    private static final long COMMIT_CLOSE_TRANSITION_TIMEOUT_MS = 1000;
     private long mMaxAnimationDuration = MAX_ANIMATION_DURATION;
     // Note: Must keep a reference when register to ValueAnimator.
     private final ValueAnimator.DurationScaleChangeListener mAnimationScaleChangeListener;
@@ -1292,9 +1294,35 @@ public class BackAnimationController implements RemoteCallable<BackAnimationCont
             if (mOnAnimationFinishCallback != null) {
                 mOnAnimationFinishCallback.run();
                 mOnAnimationFinishCallback = null;
+            } else if (mCloseTransitionRequested && mPrepareOpenTransition != null) {
+                scheduleCommitWithoutCloseRecovery(mPrepareOpenTransition);
             }
         }
 
+        /**
+         * Duo: a committed Back whose closing transition never arrives. The commit asks the app to go back and waits
+         * for the resulting closing transition while holding the prepare transition (mCloseTransitionRequested). If
+         * the app's Back changes nothing (a rejected moveTaskToBack: an activity controller veto, or a move that is a
+         * no-op), no closing transition comes, or it is aborted, and the prepare transition was never finished: core
+         * kept the animation composed, the opening target paused for touch and every later predictive Back refused.
+         * Bounded recovery: once the post-commit animation has finished, give the closing transition
+         * {@link #COMMIT_CLOSE_TRANSITION_TIMEOUT_MS}; if it has still not arrived, take the cancel path (the close
+         * prepare transition restores the launch-behind targets in core, finishes the prepare transition here, and core
+         * then clears the animation). A closing transition that arrives in time is merged as before.
+         */
+        private void scheduleCommitWithoutCloseRecovery(@NonNull IBinder prepareTransition) {
+            mShellExecutor.executeDelayed(() -> {
+                if (!mCloseTransitionRequested || mPrepareOpenTransition != prepareTransition
+                        || mOnAnimationFinishCallback != null || mClosePrepareTransition != null) {
+                    return;
+                }
+                ProtoLog.w(WM_SHELL_BACK_PREVIEW, "Back committed but no closing transition in %d ms,"
+                        + " restoring the back navigation", COMMIT_CLOSE_TRANSITION_TIMEOUT_MS);
+                mCloseTransitionRequested = false;
+                createClosePrepareTransition();
+            }, COMMIT_CLOSE_TRANSITION_TIMEOUT_MS);
+        }
+
         private void applyFinishOpenTransition() {
             if (mFinishOpenTransaction != null) {
                 final SurfaceControl.Transaction t = mFinishOpenTransaction;
